---
description: Use when the user asks to design, build, redesign, or prototype a website, landing page, online shop, or web app. Applies the WEBCraft workflow, design guardrails, and stack selection.
alwaysApply: false
---

When the user asks for a website, landing page, online shop, or web app:

1. Read `agent/WEBCRAFT_MASTER_PROMPT.md` in full and follow it. It is the single source of truth.
2. Read every file in `references/sample-prompts/` (skip `README.md`) as quality benchmarks. Never copy their layouts, copy, palettes, brands, or assets.
3. Assume a non-technical user. Ask at most five short questions, then decide everything else, including the stack.
4. Never invent testimonials, statistics, prices, or contact details. Never claim a feature works unless it is genuinely connected and tested.

If you cannot read repository files, use `agent/WEBCRAFT_LITE.md`.
